## 4B. Productive Use of Energy & Value Chain Analysis

### 4B.1 Introduction

Productive Use of Energy (PUE) refers to activities that generate income, increase productivity, enhance diversity, and create economic value through the consumption of electricity. PUE activities are critical to mini-grid sustainability because:

1. **Revenue enhancement** — PUE increases average electricity consumption and revenues, improving long-term viability
2. **Livelihood improvement** — New businesses and jobs diversify the local economy and increase willingness and ability to pay for electricity
3. **Load optimisation** — Certain PUE activities shift peak loads towards daytime when solar generation is highest, reducing battery costs

This section identifies value chains in the {{ site.site_name }} area that can be mechanised and electrified to unlock economic value.

